foot (A Wayland terminal emulator)
==================================

foot is a minimalist, portable, and fast Wayland terminal emulator for Linux
and macOS. It renders text with the fcft font library, supports the sixel and
kitty image protocols, OSC 99 notifications, and starts up quickly with a
small memory footprint. Configuration lives in a single foot.ini file (system
default /etc/xdg/foot/foot.ini, user override ~/.config/foot/foot.ini).

Upstream: https://codeberg.org/dnkl/foot
License:  MIT

DEPENDENCIES
============
Build/runtime (Slackware -current core, NOT listed in REQUIRES):
  pixman-1, wayland (+wayland-client, wayland-cursor, wayland-protocols),
  libxkbcommon, fontconfig

Requires from SlackBuilds.org / local builds (listed in REQUIRES):
  fcft    font library used by foot for text rendering (>=3.3.1, <4.0.0)
  tllist  tiny linked-list library (header-only)

The fcft, tllist and wayland-protocols packages are foot's meson wrap
dependencies; meson finds their system copies via pkg-config and does not
download or build them.

OPTIONAL DEPENDENCIES (excluded in this build for reproducibility):
  libutf8proc  - needed for grapheme-clustering. NOT installed; the build
                 pins -Dgrapheme-clustering=disabled, so foot ships without
                 grapheme-aware cursor/selection movement (matches foot's
                 auto-resolved behaviour when the lib is absent).
  libutempter  - the Linux utmp logging backend. NOT installed; the build
                 pins -Dutmp-backend=none, so foot does not log login/logout
                 to utmp/wtmp. foot runs normally without it.
  systemd      - optional; ignored (not installed).

BUILDING
========
  source ./foot.info
  wget -O foot-1.28.0.tar.gz "$DOWNLOAD"
  md5sum -c <(echo "$MD5SUM  foot-1.28.0.tar.gz")
  ./foot.SlackBuild

The build configures Meson with the final /usr prefix and disables werror
(warnings-as-errors), which foot enables by default and which breaks under
Slackware -current with newer compilers.

RUNNING
=======
  foot                      # start foot with default config
  foot --help               # list options (e.g. -e CMD to run a command)

On first install foot.ini is created from the packaged default. Edit it to
choose a theme, font, glyph width, key bindings, etc. See foot.ini.5 for
details.

KNOWN ISSUES
============
- With utmp-backend=none, login/logout sessions are not recorded in utmp.
- With grapheme-clustering disabled, combining-character clusters are not
  handled as single graphemes during cursor movement or selection.
Both can be re-enabled by installing libutempter / libutf8proc and switching
the corresponding -D option to auto/enabled, then rebuilding.
